{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T05:40:58.944385Z","id":"70b4459e14b38e954f8440a73471ecb1ece68e465ccf96a08dc1269c7bc77b0f","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs:69-76, record 9c80d2c2.\n\nStore::register_session_restoring returns the note (spec 2026-10-08 §6.7) and FeedbackWaiters::set_note keeps it in a map until the session's first feedback poll; nothing in the database records it. The watches are restored either way; only the note is lost.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:bcd348c367492f1236520aa07217d7be49d5150c","span":{"start":{"line":69},"end":{"line":76},"content_hash":"4d34e0a7296ea8660cd602c9300047b0e20c46410bd0aec30d2f7a513618e2e6"},"summary":"A restored session's note is kept in daemon memory, so a daemon restart before its first poll drops it","tags":["revisit:a session column or table for one-shot notes","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T05:40:58.944529Z","id":"93b4cf53d5e6a15422678e15d461dfd6f9a303a7ca765db3b26a1ea378d3f9b0","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs:1110-1135, record d7f95bed.\n\nholds_surface(person) (holds_owner_topics() for the owner) is true while any stream of that person holds questions or inbox, and those topics stay subscribed while the tab is hidden (web/shell/src/stream.ts:23-27). crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs create() uses it, for the asking agent's person, to decide whether a hook question waits in Clax or is released to the terminal at once. So a Clax tab left open in the background makes every AskUserQuestion of that person's agents wait in Clax until it is answered there, released, timed out, or Esc is pressed (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-agent-questions-and-inbox-design.md:289-302). Decision needed: should 'open' instead mean a tab seen or focused recently, or the extension's side panel being open?","kind":"concern","ref":"git:bcd348c367492f1236520aa07217d7be49d5150c","span":{"start":{"line":1110},"end":{"line":1135},"content_hash":"f1417fb5728fe626e2f3661ee877c6375ec81fdcca0737af7b50b1c42b623136"},"summary":"A hidden tab counts as an open Clax surface, so the AskUserQuestion hook waits in Clax","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T05:40:59.198688Z","id":"6c71e6ae114bcb19ba9d0b206ee11ba253e5ae061ff6563dacb4fda29c0394d9","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs create() releases a hook question to the terminal at once when it is about no artifact: none named, no live working record, and Store::session_artifact (crates/clax-core/src/store/watches.rs) finds no live artifact the session watches (publishing watches). So a session that has published or watched nothing asks in the terminal whatever Clax tabs are open. A session with a page still waits in Clax while a hidden owner tab holds the questions topic (holds_owner_topics, unchanged), so the question in this thread is still open. Tests: crates/clax-server/tests/api_questions.rs a_hook_question_waits_in_clax_only_once_its_session_has_a_page, a_hook_question_waits_beside_a_page_its_session_watches.","kind":"comment","references":"93b4cf53d5e6a15422678e15d461dfd6f9a303a7ca765db3b26a1ea378d3f9b0","summary":"Narrowed, not settled: a mirrored question now waits in Clax only once its session has a page","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:42:33.857802Z","id":"682c23ff248cfad275e73214081ef3414e4fb9c45af4ad4199cf9e3fd3a633e9","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs:69-76, record 9c80d2c2.\n\nStore::register_session_restoring returns the note (spec 2026-10-08 §6.7) and FeedbackWaiters::set_note keeps it in a map until the session's first feedback poll; nothing in the database records it. The watches are restored either way; only the note is lost.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":70},"end":{"line":77},"content_hash":"4d34e0a7296ea8660cd602c9300047b0e20c46410bd0aec30d2f7a513618e2e6"},"summary":"A restored session's note is kept in daemon memory, so a daemon restart before its first poll drops it","supersedes":"70b4459e14b38e954f8440a73471ecb1ece68e465ccf96a08dc1269c7bc77b0f","tags":["revisit:a session column or table for one-shot notes","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.143580Z","id":"27bb8860b0b379f1bdddab6dbe997059441a2edaf4ef2af2657ef5e73b163566","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs:1110-1135, record d7f95bed.\n\nholds_surface(person) (holds_owner_topics() for the owner) is true while any stream of that person holds questions or inbox, and those topics stay subscribed while the tab is hidden (web/shell/src/stream.ts:23-27). crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs create() uses it, for the asking agent's person, to decide whether a hook question waits in Clax or is released to the terminal at once. So a Clax tab left open in the background makes every AskUserQuestion of that person's agents wait in Clax until it is answered there, released, timed out, or Esc is pressed (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-agent-questions-and-inbox-design.md:289-302). Decision needed: should 'open' instead mean a tab seen or focused recently, or the extension's side panel being open?","kind":"concern","ref":"git:bcd348c367492f1236520aa07217d7be49d5150c","span":{"start":{"line":1402},"end":{"line":1427},"content_hash":"f1417fb5728fe626e2f3661ee877c6375ec81fdcca0737af7b50b1c42b623136"},"summary":"A hidden tab counts as an open Clax surface, so the AskUserQuestion hook waits in Clax","supersedes":"93b4cf53d5e6a15422678e15d461dfd6f9a303a7ca765db3b26a1ea378d3f9b0","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/live_layers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.385790Z","id":"b69a30c48f3258161c91da659f1cbef0b99eb1ffa868ab5a7a749dd5cf16c7b0","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/live_layers.rs:21-22, record 851438fc.\n\nA batch carries every changed sender whole for a receiver that is behind: with 30 detailed senders each holding a cursor near MAX_LIVE_MESSAGE_BYTES (16 KiB) and a 2000-character draft, one batch is several hundred KiB, and SOCKET_QUEUE (16) of them can wait behind a receiver whose socket does not drain, so a few MiB per stalled socket, per artifact, before try_send drops the next one and marks it for a whole resend. Bounded, but more than needed: a lost batch is already answered with full state (Relay::resend).","kind":"concern","ref":"git:e41ba8925faa9431a1414ae995a711f31b3c5343","span":{"start":{"line":21},"end":{"line":22},"content_hash":"152e995d6c246399649d0054fe7ebb59abc2d37fc3a650bfabec7652df161c8a"},"suggested_fix":"Lower SOCKET_QUEUE to a few batches (the full-state resend covers what is dropped), or cap a batch's bytes and resend the rest at the next flush.","summary":"A stalled receiver may hold up to 16 queued batches, each up to about 30 senders' largest cursors and drafts","tags":["live-layers","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/seats.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.844258Z","id":"7d33e1bdecbbec66eb1fcb4df43c2d2713bb8d7c26061bb7f329723e03871b49","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/seats.rs:210-215, record d5a80748.\n\nThe native daemon has no per-artifact live socket like the hosted prototype's /api/artifacts/:id/live (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts fetch); the shell's one shared stream subscribing an artifact's artifact, presence or working topic holds the seat (crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs use_seats, crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs update). A live relay of pointers, selections and typing on another connection asks LiveSeats::is_seated, or holds a seat itself with LiveSeats::take and leave under its own connection key and hears idle releases through LiveSeats::on_idle; nothing natively takes an agent seat yet, as agents hold no live connection here.","kind":"alternative","ref":"git:217836344261c10bd08dc555b813e6df2823eb7c","span":{"start":{"line":198},"end":{"line":203},"content_hash":"32ceb5fbc1090c840186b68a86c8d81947c5c3f81c3c2528455f8ab93d97ec23"},"summary":"Seats are held by /api/stream subscriptions, not by a live socket of their own","tags":["revisit:a live relay socket lands beside /api/stream","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:34.844788Z","id":"fdd2ac89b194f67d0c21e21638c9585b81ff9ab6de642692743a477717b3a940","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs:1402-1427, record dc390190.\n\nholds_surface(person) (holds_owner_topics() for the owner) is true while any stream of that person holds questions or inbox, and those topics stay subscribed while the tab is hidden (web/shell/src/stream.ts:23-27). crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs create() uses it, for the asking agent's person, to decide whether a hook question waits in Clax or is released to the terminal at once. So a Clax tab left open in the background makes every AskUserQuestion of that person's agents wait in Clax until it is answered there, released, timed out, or Esc is pressed (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-agent-questions-and-inbox-design.md:289-302). Decision needed: should 'open' instead mean a tab seen or focused recently, or the extension's side panel being open?","kind":"concern","ref":"git:bcd348c367492f1236520aa07217d7be49d5150c","span":{"start":{"line":1402},"end":{"line":1427},"content_hash":"f1417fb5728fe626e2f3661ee877c6375ec81fdcca0737af7b50b1c42b623136"},"summary":"A hidden tab counts as an open Clax surface, so the AskUserQuestion hook waits in Clax","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/seats.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:42:17.874027Z","id":"e1956861616f4ed5734620176bc6383192ad7d1f836bfcab06ae75fa465bf620","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"7d33e1bdecbbec66eb1fcb4df43c2d2713bb8d7c26061bb7f329723e03871b49","summary":"The hosted/ files this record cites were removed in 60298c1d (the TypeScript prototype's retirement); read one at its parent with git show 60298c1d^:hosted/<path>","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:42:17.930505Z","id":"1ed6953fb52593ed53c2b90f4eb11811ba631b7458391b20998835e23b7fa7fd","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs create() releases a hook question to the terminal at once when it is about no artifact: none named, no live working record, and Store::session_artifact (crates/clax-core/src/store/watches.rs) finds no live artifact the session watches (publishing watches). So a session that has published or watched nothing asks in the terminal whatever Clax tabs are open. A session with a page still waits in Clax while a hidden owner tab holds the questions topic (holds_owner_topics, unchanged), so the question in this thread is still open. Tests: crates/clax-server/tests/api_questions.rs a_hook_question_waits_in_clax_only_once_its_session_has_a_page, a_hook_question_waits_beside_a_page_its_session_watches.","kind":"comment","references":"fdd2ac89b194f67d0c21e21638c9585b81ff9ab6de642692743a477717b3a940","summary":"Narrowed, not settled: a mirrored question now waits in Clax only once its session has a page","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:45:32.469419Z","id":"ad3bcddcf46939978336ee9e12ce6ce4e21181e5b3c072c98376d6e63c6decdf","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"The same record as 27bb8860 at crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs:1402, kept: this head is a re-anchor of it made on a branch while main moved it there","supersedes":"fdd2ac89b194f67d0c21e21638c9585b81ff9ab6de642692743a477717b3a940","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:49:31.121945Z","id":"ce49eb130eeb6cfda8f5a9ea66ca91c8fd5693a7446281f7716a8a7f39bb883b","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/feedback.rs:610-610, record b9b36f2e.\n\nFailure: an anonymous GET /api/events?artifact=<aid> receives feedback_state {state: withheld, approver: 'Sam'} after the owner sends a LAN viewer's thread to Sam's agent; a LAN viewer's thread card reads 'waiting for Sam's approval'. Spec 2026-10-08 section 18 gives a LAN viewer no approvals view; section 10 asks for the delivery state to read 'waiting for Sam's approval' without saying for whom. This predates bb547990, which makes the state more frequent (state_of now reads any held row). A question for the owner whether LAN viewers should see 'waiting for approval' without the name.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:bcd348c367492f1236520aa07217d7be49d5150c","span":{"start":{"line":577},"end":{"line":583},"content_hash":"2cbe6c4dd3392d87be3098e5f2f105a7512d467b7c6d8e24dd9619a167ac3b57"},"summary":"feedback_state.approver names whose approval a thread waits for to LAN viewers and anonymous event subscribers","tags":["review","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:49:44.565585Z","id":"edc8c75c17c1f2262f3771d59827c381cf14085e5adeb4cbc6720e166fe9437b","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"ce49eb130eeb6cfda8f5a9ea66ca91c8fd5693a7446281f7716a8a7f39bb883b","summary":"Ruling (2026-10-13, from spec section 18: LAN viewers see no approvals): feedback_state.approver stays out of LAN viewers' and anonymous callers' views and out of event streams; the owner and the people concerned (the approver, the thread's own authors, and their agents) keep it.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:52:20.536930Z","id":"7c01451860f1464fbed391a85c7835743add41f89a05bfdd5cb90dc5bc33f805","body":{"detail":"The in-memory halves moved to clax-realtime: LiveSeats (seats.rs), the GitRemotes host and its Slot (git_remotes.rs), and linked threads' Linked state (linked.rs), because clax-realtime's stream hub and FeedbackCtx hold them and may not depend on clax-http. The rules that read a request (claiming a seat for a Caller, minting and settling tokens, the sync task) stay above. Linked's fields are pub for the sync task in clax-server. The alternative is trait objects the HTTP layer installs into the realtime types.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":11},"end":{"line":19},"content_hash":"da10fded101b218ccb74c935368c7cfc61a28d50133b67cfa1a4ec6d5b728c2a"},"summary":"Keep live seats, git remotes and linked threads' state whole in clax-http, inverting what the stream hub and feedback fan-out need of them","tags":["layout","revisit:a realtime type needs more of these halves than their state","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:52:20.537043Z","id":"5a294594dce81a5de7e88452e58e989db939a038ee78d98626d3de0d468c9a83","body":{"detail":"Conn::holding takes any Send + Sync guard (Box<dyn Any>) because socket_caps (counting connections per client, answering 429 with ApiError) is clax-http's, which clax-realtime may not name. The guard's only job is to be dropped with the connection.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1621},"end":{"line":1626},"content_hash":"cca2553b03a64c14e63a4a6d829f6c07b4c0bd15dc02558347ef71d1fcc312f3"},"summary":"A stream connection holds its socket slot as any guard, not as socket_caps::SocketSlot","tags":["layout","revisit:the stream needs to read its slot","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:15:03.302231Z","id":"c3176d433420f5c72308f2a82304b91585101cc36ebdc60f069cbc901e8b4b71","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d41601bde","summary":"A hidden tab no longer counts as Clax attention: the AskUserQuestion hook's mode in crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs create() follows the session's suggestion (clax_http::surface::suggestion in crates/clax-http/src/surface.rs, clax_core::surface::suggest in crates/clax-core/src/surface.rs), in which only a focused tab or input on the session's page counts as engagement; Hub::holds_surface (crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs:1414-1422) now only says whether Clax can show a question. This also answers reply 6c71e6ae: a session with a page no longer waits in Clax because a hidden owner tab holds the questions topic. Evidence: bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:all --test_arg=api_questions::a_hidden_tab_does_not_hold_a_hook_question_after_a_prompt --test_arg=api_where_to_ask::a_hidden_tab_is_not_engagement passes (each 'ok', 1 passed; 7 out of 7 test targets pass).","supersedes":"27bb8860b0b379f1bdddab6dbe997059441a2edaf4ef2af2657ef5e73b163566","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:21:07.456888Z","id":"7a74d43f50a1e0a946b2dceebb19f866489841563912887d3190573b75de7376","body":{"detail":"Conn::holding takes any Send + Sync guard (Box<dyn Any>) because socket_caps (counting connections per client, answering 429 with ApiError) is clax-http's, which clax-realtime may not name. The guard's only job is to be dropped with the connection.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1637},"end":{"line":1642},"content_hash":"cca2553b03a64c14e63a4a6d829f6c07b4c0bd15dc02558347ef71d1fcc312f3"},"summary":"A stream connection holds its socket slot as any guard, not as socket_caps::SocketSlot","supersedes":"5a294594dce81a5de7e88452e58e989db939a038ee78d98626d3de0d468c9a83","tags":["layout","revisit:the stream needs to read its slot","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:58:52.885185Z","id":"8a26d21fb4c0bcae2fedfb6e2e04ce208ff47f9e35e6c884b04fd1573b0d0ff6","body":{"detail":"Hub::unseat removes the artifact's live topics from the stream and leaves their channels, then offers `unseated` with a bare `tx.try_send(...)`; on TrySendError::Full the frame is discarded and nothing else records it (no entry in Shared::lagged, no notify), unlike Hub::dispatch (stream.rs:1023-1033), which marks a full queue behind and sends `resync`. The seat is released for want of input (crates/clax-http/src/seats.rs:188 calls unseat with IDLE_CODE), which is exactly when a backgrounded tab is least likely to be reading its stream. The page then keeps believing it holds `artifact:<id>`, `presence:<id>` and `working:<id>`, receives none of their events, and never turns spectator; if one of those topics had already fallen behind, take_lagged later sends `resync` for a topic the stream no longer holds, so the page refetches and still waits on a dead subscription. The resume path (stream.rs:1121-1141) does put `unseated` in the prelude, so only a stream attached at the moment of the release is affected.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":936},"end":{"line":944},"content_hash":"ab27ef52f122e00eee4b920153cf4ca5d3d5ebcd8ea6201c46c3fd1f5d7f6084"},"suggested_fix":"When the try_send fails with Full, record the unseat out of band as lag is recorded: push it to a per-stream list in Shared (or a dedicated `unseated` list) and notify, and have Conn::next/Conn::drain emit the `unseated` frames from it before anything else; add a test that fills a stream's queue, unseats it, and asserts the frame arrives.","summary":"Hub::unseat drops the `unseated` frame when the stream's queue is full, so the page is never told it left the artifact's live topics","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/room.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:58:52.885229Z","id":"d0a2ce373dfbe6c0da33f6d6a63a67b057f9ee4d2f5aa4d879fadb6d98c00eda","body":{"detail":"The peer label is chosen by the page (`?peer=`, checked only for shape by peer_label_ok in crates/clax-server/src/routes/room.rs:166-171) and is shown to every other member in each `peer` frame (Sender::render, room.rs:55-66). Rooms::claim (room.rs:139-153) inserts the new socket's Notify under (artifact, label) and wakes the old one, which closes 4409 `replaced` (routes/room.rs:448-450); Rooms::enter (room.rs:172) drops the old entry of that label from the room with no `left`. Neither compares Who::viewer. So any viewer who can open the room (a LAN viewer, a hosted guest) can, by reconnecting with a label it has seen, disconnect another person's socket, and keep doing so as that socket reconnects with its stored label, while the room sees one upsert as if the same peer had changed rather than a different person arriving. The replace rule is meant for one tab reconnecting (module docs, room.rs:11-15).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":139},"end":{"line":153},"content_hash":"ba02d30f69f542b96e8a4c1954088bf78e42f8004acb2e593d3dc634139f46d0"},"suggested_fix":"Bind a label to the viewer that first claimed it: store the claimant's viewer (or, for an anonymous socket, a per-connection secret) with the Notify in Inner::claims, and in claim/enter refuse (close with a distinct code, or treat as a new label) a claim from a different viewer while the label is held; only a socket of the same viewer replaces it. Add a test where viewer B claims viewer A's label and A's socket is not woken.","summary":"Any room member can take another socket's peer label: Rooms::claim and Rooms::enter key the label by artifact alone, so the older socket is closed `replaced` whoever the newcomer is","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/live_layers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:58:52.885270Z","id":"957241055ebc9413e0e0fe36f507b22af3ef9476be28b37933de62eb22dde184","body":{"detail":"In LiveLayers::flush a TrySendError::Full calls room.relay.resend(key), which sets Relay::dirty (crates/clax-core/src/live_layers.rs:505-508); Self::arm then sees pending() and returns true, and flush schedules itself again (live_layers.rs:306-308). A receiver that never reads (a stalled client, or a socket task blocked on a slow write) therefore keeps one spawned task and one Relay::batches pass, re-serialising its whole batch, every 100 ms until the socket closes, even when no sender changed anything. On a host that wakes for timers (the Durable Object host this module's on_queue serves) this also keeps the instance awake. The open thread on live_layers.rs:21-22 covers the memory a stalled receiver holds, not this timer loop.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":291},"end":{"line":308},"content_hash":"15b36a7234449aa03032cb4c99f1cf28859e73638272a430a3913a556e3d9fda"},"suggested_fix":"Mark the stalled socket as owed a whole batch without arming a timer: keep a per-socket `owed` flag set on Full and cleared on a successful send, have the socket's writer (or the drain path) request a flush once its queue has room again, and arm the timer only when the relay has news from a sender. A test can fill a socket's queue, call flush, and assert no further flush is scheduled while nothing changes.","summary":"A live socket whose queue stays full re-arms its artifact's flush every FLUSH_MS (100 ms) for as long as it stays open","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:58:52.885353Z","id":"0130cb6d2da027f788ff45930dc464af96aa850cc0941da0f31b18a5d6c3be78","body":{"detail":"Topic::name maps both variants to `artifact:<id>`, but they are different keys of StreamEntry::topics, and Hub::update_via (stream.rs:1305-1324) only skips a topic already held by equality. The subscription route picks the variant per request (crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs:448-454, from hosted::reads_comments) and removes both only on unsubscribe (routes/stream.rs:369-374). A browser's one shared stream carries every tab's topics (stream.rs:52-54), so a second tab subscribing after the person's comment right changed adds the other variant: the stream then holds two `artifact:<id>` topics, `version`, `working`, `agents` and `feedback_state` events arrive once per variant (routes() at stream.rs:609-626 files them in both channels), `ready.topics` lists the name twice, and Conn::dropped and clear_lag, keyed by name, conflate the two. The open thread on routes/stream.rs:448-454 is about when the variant is decided, not about holding both.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":141},"end":{"line":145},"content_hash":"3ed51897ebf030b215ad2abc70a552b83630fff300250d4cbe8bc582cf6e0b9e"},"suggested_fix":"In Hub::update_via, when adding Artifact(a) or ArtifactQuiet(a), first remove the other variant of the same artifact (leaving its channels) so a stream holds at most one; or give the quiet variant its own channel-set but a single Topic key. Add a test that subscribes Artifact then ArtifactQuiet of one artifact and asserts one `version` frame per event.","summary":"One stream can hold both Topic::Artifact and Topic::ArtifactQuiet of one artifact, which share the name `artifact:<id>`, and then receives each non-thread event twice","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:12.260722Z","id":"38349b0a958c8cbd773143e2876281b4c22717ad2f0403657c2c133c2a4a08ad","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs:929-944 removes each live topic, leaves its channels, then `tx.try_send(Arc::new(unseated_item(..))).is_ok()`; on Full nothing is recorded. Hub::dispatch (:1022-1033) on Full sets sub.lagged, pushes to shared.lagged and notifies. crates/clax-http/src/seats.rs:188 calls hub.unseat(id, &r.artifact, IDLE_CODE) from the seats on_idle callback. The resume path (stream.rs:1121-1141) does emit unseated frames in its prelude, so only an attached stream with a full queue loses it. Concern fits.","kind":"comment","references":"8a26d21fb4c0bcae2fedfb6e2e04ce208ff47f9e35e6c884b04fd1573b0d0ff6","summary":"confirmed: Hub::unseat drops the `unseated` frame on a full queue with no lag record","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/room.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:12.260881Z","id":"b45a30ded7921d7d1fba7925ff4a9753fb31c3e3de466f6205724effcb5b8bb5","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-realtime/src/room.rs:139-153 Rooms::claim inserts under (aid, peer) and notifies the old Notify unconditionally; enter (:157-189) runs `r.members.retain(|_, (w, _)| w.peer != who.peer)` with no viewer comparison. Labels are broadcast to members (Sender::render, :55-66, `peer: who.peer.clone()`). The route checks the label only for shape (crates/clax-server/src/routes/room.rs:166-171) and closes 4409 `replaced` when notified (:446-450). The module docs (room.rs:11-15) frame replacement as one socket's reconnect. Concern fits.","kind":"comment","references":"d0a2ce373dfbe6c0da33f6d6a63a67b057f9ee4d2f5aa4d879fadb6d98c00eda","summary":"confirmed: claim and enter key labels by artifact alone, so any member can displace another viewer's socket","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/live_layers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:12.261039Z","id":"fb18c1ed80cb006638ed2061759a4351e1860e8c25523f2d3058704f5320b76a","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-realtime/src/live_layers.rs:291-308: on TrySendError::Full flush calls room.relay.resend(key), which removes sent[socket] and sets dirty = true (crates/clax-core/src/live_layers.rs:503-508); Self::arm (:249-254) returns true while relay.pending() (dirty), and flush then calls schedule (:306-308), which sleeps flush_after and flushes again. Because sent[socket] was cleared, the next Relay::batches yields a whole batch for that socket again whenever it has any sender, which fails Full again, so the loop repeats until the socket drains or closes. Concern fits.","kind":"comment","references":"957241055ebc9413e0e0fe36f507b22af3ef9476be28b37933de62eb22dde184","summary":"confirmed: a full live socket re-arms the artifact's flush every FLUSH_MS while it stays full","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:12.261193Z","id":"ecde4f45f034481de45d0cebf3a8856a29fb50c98beb5201975d9797b9038484","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs:141-145 maps Topic::Artifact(a) and Topic::ArtifactQuiet(a) to `artifact:{a}`; Hub::update_via (:1305-1307) skips only `s.topics.contains_key(t)`, an exact key match. routes() (:608-626) files every non-thread event on both Chan::Artifact and Chan::ArtifactQuiet. crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs:448-454 picks the variant per request from hosted::reads_comments, and only unsubscribe adds both variants (:369-374). update_via returns `s.topics.keys().map(Topic::name)` (:1324), which would list the name twice. Concern fits.","kind":"comment","references":"0130cb6d2da027f788ff45930dc464af96aa850cc0941da0f31b18a5d6c3be78","summary":"confirmed: a stream can hold both Artifact and ArtifactQuiet of one artifact under one name","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/room.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:08:51.161094Z","id":"dbc53c23657dccde4a648667b90d72e9c38434b669ce8efe93e5b8734116cafa","body":{"detail":"Binding a peer label to its viewer changes a documented contract and collides with a documented reconnect flow, so the fix needs the owner's choice. Facts the choice rests on:\n\n- docs/contract.md \"Close codes\" says 4409 `replaced` is sent when \"a newer socket took this label; it is never refused\". Refusing a claim changes that promise.\n- The shell reuses a document's label across reconnects, including \"when the viewer's name changes\" (docs/contract.md, \"The socket\"). On a viewer change web/shell/src/caps/room.ts (the `viewers(...)` handler, about lines 214-224) opens the new socket while the old one is still open and closes the old one only once the new one opens (`retired`, onopen). So a new socket under a held label may legitimately come from a different `Who::viewer` (an anonymous tab that is now named, or a viewer folded into the owner).\n- The impact is larger than the root says: web/shell/src/caps/room.ts:191 treats 4409 as terminal (`terminal = true`, no reconnect), so one displacement ends the victim document's room until the page reloads; there is no fight over reconnects.\n- Anonymous sockets (`viewer: None`) cannot be told apart by viewer at all.\n\nOptions:\nA. Refuse a claim from a different viewer while the label is held (close with a new code, e.g. 4409 `taken`, or reuse 4403). Simple; changes the contract; breaks the viewer-change reconnect above whenever the viewer ID differs (the new socket is refused while the retired one is open, and the shell keeps retrying). Anonymous-vs-anonymous stays displaceable unless also refused, which breaks anonymous reconnect over a half-open socket.\nB. Give the newcomer a fresh server-picked label instead of refusing (the welcome frame already carries `peer`). Keeps \"never refused\"; the shell must adopt the label from `welcome` instead of assuming its own, and the room sees a new peer plus a `left` instead of one upsert on a viewer change.\nC. Per-document secret: the shell sends, with the label, a random secret it keeps with the label; a claim replaces a held label only with the same secret. Covers anonymous sockets and viewer changes alike; needs a protocol change in the shell, the bridge contract and both hosts (crates/clax-server/src/routes/room.rs `room_socket` and `RoomSocket::open`).\n\nRecommendation: C. It is the only option that keeps one tab's reconnect working across viewer changes and anonymous sockets while making a label unguessable to other members; until it lands, A restricted to two different named viewers (both `Some` and unequal) closes the cross-person case with the least breakage.","kind":"comment","references":"d0a2ce373dfbe6c0da33f6d6a63a67b057f9ee4d2f5aa4d879fadb6d98c00eda","summary":"Needs a decision: binding a label to its viewer changes the 'never refused' 4409 contract and collides with the shell's viewer-change reconnect","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/live_layers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:22:30.823887Z","id":"c9817182cbe81b3c14deac27162be7f78bbc8f8efe46307f11f4d449dbc4dbbf","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:5c0e059f7","summary":"Fixed: a full queue marks the socket owed (Relay::forget) and one waiter per socket re-arms a single flush once tx.reserve() has room; a_full_queue_arms_no_flush_until_it_has_room passes (failed before), 30/30 uncached runs.","supersedes":"957241055ebc9413e0e0fe36f507b22af3ef9476be28b37933de62eb22dde184","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:22:30.857352Z","id":"7821a15399ba842e83521da13e601da914d58dd7ce7cb2b75b46cee5f12713a2","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:aa293620e","summary":"Fixed: subscribing to either artifact:<id> variant leaves the other and MAX_TOPICS counts by name; an_artifact_topic_is_held_loud_or_quiet_never_both passes (failed before).","supersedes":"0130cb6d2da027f788ff45930dc464af96aa850cc0941da0f31b18a5d6c3be78","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:22:30.904442Z","id":"52dd86ef9cdead62e780c63d6ce5989572237f94347eb7a3edf06f9ddd67ab33","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:91fadf597","summary":"Fixed: on a full queue the unseated frame is stored on shared state and sent before queued frames, skipping the left topic's events; a_full_queue_still_hears_it_was_unseated_and_no_resync_after passes (failed before).","supersedes":"8a26d21fb4c0bcae2fedfb6e2e04ce208ff47f9e35e6c884b04fd1573b0d0ff6","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:53:17.992849Z","id":"5634d45436d4e0ccdc7a27ce1fbbc1ccc272a121e2c67fae6e223b2bae724ad9","body":{"detail":"Event::Tags { artifact_id: None } routes to Chan::Gallery alone. On a hosted Clax the gate drops the gallery topic for a member whose rights do not read every artifact (crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs member_gate, 'Topic::Gallery if !every => continue'), and an artifact page subscribes only artifact:<aid>. Such a member's open pages and gallery therefore keep showing a deleted tag or the old name until reload, though the contract (docs/contract.md, the 'tags' event) says clients refetch on it. crates/clax-store/src/tags.rs delete_tag returns the carriers' IDs, which crates/clax-server/src/routes/tags.rs:213-220 drops.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":732},"end":{"line":739},"content_hash":"eebfd046da0dc979430584c64928999de70b501595e69e15e11e2c8c5c06b428"},"suggested_fix":"On a delete, publish Event::Tags { artifact_id: Some(aid) } for each carrier delete_tag returns; for a rename, either the same (the carriers from artifact_tags_by_tag) or a topic every signed-in person may hold that names nothing.","summary":"A tag renamed, recoloured or deleted reaches only the gallery topic, which a hosted member with partial rights never holds","tags":["review","review:artifact-tags","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:55:11.179198Z","id":"3bf802db2eeae5ef0e9238e92af0299eef7be91ad313c305c15dc67481cc3f34","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs:734-739 routes Event::Tags { artifact_id: None } to vec![(Chan::Gallery, Gate::Any)] only. crates/clax-http/src/hosted.rs:1052-1058 computes every = rights.allows(Artifacts, read, None, ..) and skips Topic::Gallery when !every. crates/clax-server/src/routes/tags.rs:213-223 (delete) publishes Event::Tags { artifact_id: None } and returns only carried.len(), discarding the carrier IDs that crates/clax-store/src/tags.rs:280-303 delete_tag returns.","kind":"comment","references":"5634d45436d4e0ccdc7a27ce1fbbc1ccc272a121e2c67fae6e223b2bae724ad9","summary":"confirmed: list-wide tag events go to the gallery channel only, which the hosted gate drops for partial-rights members","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:14:34.627734Z","id":"c5b09c367809cdaadd5fe49562bf6e9a811be19b760427cbeb93267c04ef37e5","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e62a94b0c","summary":"Fixed in e62a94b0c: a rename, recolour or delete also reaches each carrier's artifact topic, naming the artifact (Event::Tags carriers, Store::tag_carriers); stream::tests::tag_changes_reach_the_gallery_and_the_artifacts_topic and api_hosted::a_members_page_hears_a_tag_it_carries_renamed_or_deleted (a member whose stream holds no gallery) pass (bazelisk test //crates/clax-realtime:all //crates/clax-server:all PASSED)","supersedes":"5634d45436d4e0ccdc7a27ce1fbbc1ccc272a121e2c67fae6e223b2bae724ad9","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/room.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T18:09:13.419654Z","id":"a50ae6abf36c74b5599e652ef4a764ad8361241c646dea140d3615ed46e03f13","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"d0a2ce373dfbe6c0da33f6d6a63a67b057f9ee4d2f5aa4d879fadb6d98c00eda","summary":"Bound since: Rooms::claim takes the claiming viewer and answers None while another viewer's socket holds the label, and the room route closes the newcomer 4403 peer_taken (crates/clax-server/src/routes/room.rs session and RoomSocket::open; tests crates/clax-realtime/src/room.rs another_viewer_never_takes_a_label, crates/clax-server/tests/api_room.rs another_viewer_cannot_take_a_label). 4409 replaced is now for the same viewer alone. The shell's viewer-change reconnect keeps its label; a new viewer is refused it and takes a fresh label (web/shell/src/caps/room.ts, test 'a label another viewer holds is given up for a fresh one, quietly'), so peers see it leave and enter instead of a seamless swap. Anonymous sockets (no viewer) still replace each other.","tags":["session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/room.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:38:55.584582Z","id":"0af48dbc02153b64316de9ae107202e6ed8fa4877234bcedb61f3b9fa461905a","body":{"detail":"The peer label is chosen by the page (`?peer=`, checked only for shape by peer_label_ok in crates/clax-server/src/routes/room.rs:166-171) and is shown to every other member in each `peer` frame (Sender::render, room.rs:55-66). Rooms::claim (room.rs:139-153) inserts the new socket's Notify under (artifact, label) and wakes the old one, which closes 4409 `replaced` (routes/room.rs:448-450); Rooms::enter (room.rs:172) drops the old entry of that label from the room with no `left`. Neither compares Who::viewer. So any viewer who can open the room (a LAN viewer, a hosted guest) can, by reconnecting with a label it has seen, disconnect another person's socket, and keep doing so as that socket reconnects with its stored label, while the room sees one upsert as if the same peer had changed rather than a different person arriving. The replace rule is meant for one tab reconnecting (module docs, room.rs:11-15).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":139},"end":{"line":153},"content_hash":"e1005c722feb171ed9670710321ef5f2ad344a527a6efc9784434083f44f81cd"},"suggested_fix":"Bind a label to the viewer that first claimed it: store the claimant's viewer (or, for an anonymous socket, a per-connection secret) with the Notify in Inner::claims, and in claim/enter refuse (close with a distinct code, or treat as a new label) a claim from a different viewer while the label is held; only a socket of the same viewer replaces it. Add a test where viewer B claims viewer A's label and A's socket is not woken.","summary":"Any room member can take another socket's peer label: Rooms::claim and Rooms::enter key the label by artifact alone, so the older socket is closed `replaced` whoever the newcomer is","supersedes":"d0a2ce373dfbe6c0da33f6d6a63a67b057f9ee4d2f5aa4d879fadb6d98c00eda","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:44.374447Z","id":"ecd917c6dbe4ddbb38ba39fc26329989eddbbdb9b222be9df3768bc44bfd33b6","body":{"detail":"Conn::holding takes any Send + Sync guard (Box<dyn Any>) because socket_caps (counting connections per client, answering 429 with ApiError) is clax-http's, which clax-realtime may not name. The guard's only job is to be dropped with the connection.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs:1637:1642 to crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs:1998:2003: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1998},"end":{"line":2003},"content_hash":"cca2553b03a64c14e63a4a6d829f6c07b4c0bd15dc02558347ef71d1fcc312f3"},"summary":"A stream connection holds its socket slot as any guard, not as socket_caps::SocketSlot","supersedes":"7a74d43f50a1e0a946b2dceebb19f866489841563912887d3190573b75de7376","tags":["layout","revisit:the stream needs to read its slot","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T01:44:08.740351Z","id":"9c6c1392c2b277ba376d964577a37a1aae09dc32154f241800c785a3d3af5a8a","body":{"detail":"Conn::holding takes any Send + Sync guard (Box<dyn Any>) because socket_caps (counting connections per client, answering 429 with ApiError) is clax-http's, which clax-realtime may not name. The guard's only job is to be dropped with the connection.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs:1637:1642 to crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs:1998:2003: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2000},"end":{"line":2005},"content_hash":"cca2553b03a64c14e63a4a6d829f6c07b4c0bd15dc02558347ef71d1fcc312f3"},"summary":"A stream connection holds its socket slot as any guard, not as socket_caps::SocketSlot","supersedes":"ecd917c6dbe4ddbb38ba39fc26329989eddbbdb9b222be9df3768bc44bfd33b6","tags":["layout","revisit:the stream needs to read its slot","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T14:57:11.017853Z","id":"e01539ae15c8ac136c0e3aea939db8f99f08dfd8dc4fa498e236ef222fffa3c6","body":{"detail":"Conn::holding takes any Send + Sync guard (Box<dyn Any>) because socket_caps (counting connections per client, answering 429 with ApiError) is clax-http's, which clax-realtime may not name. The guard's only job is to be dropped with the connection.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs:1637:1642 to crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs:1998:2003: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2002},"end":{"line":2007},"content_hash":"cca2553b03a64c14e63a4a6d829f6c07b4c0bd15dc02558347ef71d1fcc312f3"},"summary":"A stream connection holds its socket slot as any guard, not as socket_caps::SocketSlot","supersedes":"9c6c1392c2b277ba376d964577a37a1aae09dc32154f241800c785a3d3af5a8a","tags":["layout","revisit:the stream needs to read its slot","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T03:36:58.675963Z","id":"1f31be7456972faa4d27586554ec53a6d44eaf908e5fa79f1e696c99cf407b23","body":{"detail":"Conn::holding takes any Send + Sync guard (Box<dyn Any>) because socket_caps (counting connections per client, answering 429 with ApiError) is clax-http's, which clax-realtime may not name. The guard's only job is to be dropped with the connection.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs:1637:1642 to crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs:1998:2003: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2005},"end":{"line":2010},"content_hash":"cca2553b03a64c14e63a4a6d829f6c07b4c0bd15dc02558347ef71d1fcc312f3"},"summary":"A stream connection holds its socket slot as any guard, not as socket_caps::SocketSlot","supersedes":"e01539ae15c8ac136c0e3aea939db8f99f08dfd8dc4fa498e236ef222fffa3c6","tags":["layout","revisit:the stream needs to read its slot","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-realtime/src/live_layers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:18.682674Z","id":"8c29a989d0224020a24264d9db444c83095a9f2986ca6fac8ac2f836845b2a89","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-server/src/live_layers.rs:21-22, record 851438fc.\n\nA batch carries every changed sender whole for a receiver that is behind: with 30 detailed senders each holding a cursor near MAX_LIVE_MESSAGE_BYTES (16 KiB) and a 2000-character draft, one batch is several hundred KiB, and SOCKET_QUEUE (16) of them can wait behind a receiver whose socket does not drain, so a few MiB per stalled socket, per artifact, before try_send drops the next one and marks it for a whole resend. Bounded, but more than needed: a lost batch is already answered with full state (Relay::resend).\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":23},"end":{"line":24},"content_hash":"152e995d6c246399649d0054fe7ebb59abc2d37fc3a650bfabec7652df161c8a"},"suggested_fix":"Lower SOCKET_QUEUE to a few batches (the full-state resend covers what is dropped), or cap a batch's bytes and resend the rest at the next flush.","summary":"A stalled receiver may hold up to 16 queued batches, each up to about 30 senders' largest cursors and drafts","supersedes":"b69a30c48f3258161c91da659f1cbef0b99eb1ffa868ab5a7a749dd5cf16c7b0","tags":["live-layers","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
